{"author":{"id":"1832e4168d45d4ef31531146dbc743bb950a5dd543b15fd8e3a076fd976bfdef"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960750,"nonce":"V2lx/YKlgPQfnZARFKN2C1qJ5qc=","title":"declarations are read from a file path, so every caller writes a temporary file","message":"`generate_*`, `web_backend*` and `haxe::generate` take the declaration as `Option\u003cPathBuf\u003e`. Every caller holds it as text (`include_str!`, or text with generated enums appended), so each writes it to a temporary file first: xgpu's `_haxe` uses a fixed `temp_dir()/gpu.api.rs`, which parallel builds overwrite under each other; cb_gpu, hlwgpu and rayzor-gpu stamp file names with the time. Taking the declaration's text removes the files and the race.","files":null}]}